    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on wolfram2002-ch01-01: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.33";
    dc:description "The claim has empirical implications only after choosing model classes and domains. Existing data can compare such models in examples, but cannot resolve the unrestricted assertion about rules throughout nature.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/mixed";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Define classes of equation-based and program-based models for selected natural systems and compare their out-of-sample fit and complexity penalties. Consistent superiority of program models would support the claim for those systems, but not establish the unrestricted principle.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Available datasets cannot represent all natural systems.", "The boundary between equations and programs is not mathematically sharp.";
